invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide.c
catches: x25519_equiv_test
reason: each step swaps the points once, by the step's scalar bit exclusive-or
  the bit of the step before, since the step no longer swaps them back at
  its end (docs/decisions.md 152). A swap by the bit alone leaves them
  swapped after every step whose bit is 1, which changes the result for
  nearly every scalar, and the comparison with the 16-word field sees it.

--- old
        step(a, b, c, d, e, f, x, bit ^ r);
--- new
        step(a, b, c, d, e, f, x, r);
